CodexBar status item placement preservation — native AppKit proof
Verified 2026-09-18 on macOS 27.0, arm64, 2880x1620 logical display.

Harness:
- Compiled the production preservation/preflight helpers into a standalone
  NSApplication accessory app signed with the matching Developer ID.
- Unique bundle/defaults domain; one synthetic item labeled "CB Proof".
- Seeded preferred position 600; no settings store, provider startup,
  credentials, browser sessions, or real account content.
- Verified the item visibly on screen. ScreenCaptureKit preparation timed out;
  Peekaboo's classic capture succeeded. Full desktop captures stayed local;
  shared crops contain only the synthetic item.

Before:
- Raw removeStatusItem immediately changed saved position 600 to missing.
- The submitted preserve/restore helper restored 600 synchronously, but after
  recreation and release of the retired item, the value was missing again.

After:
- Reset the retired item's autosave name inside the preservation closure before
  removing it. AppKit's later cleanup can no longer clear the stable name.
- Preserved removal: 600 immediately, 600 after recreation/release and 2 seconds.
- Hide/show: 600 while hidden, 600 after showing and 2 seconds.
- Item frame remained x=1740, y=1590, width=74, height=30 in AppKit coordinates
  through recreation and hide/show; the captured item was inside the display.
- Removal before NSApplication.terminate: 600 before exit and on disk afterward.
- Fresh process launched without reseeding: saved position remained 600.

Deterministic coverage uses InMemoryUserDefaults. The two original ordinary
SwiftPM tests that created NSStatusBar.system items were removed; removal was
vacuous in that host and did not cover the delayed cleanup found above.

Scope: this verifies the native helper's real lifecycle and the controller
call sites. It does not reproduce Sequoia's older out-of-range positions in
issue #3355, so that broader issue remains open.
